OL,3,GNEWSAEngineer aims to lift world
OL,4,Astrongman title
OL,5,
OL,6,FA strongman says he aims "to win" when
OL,7,Fhe represents England in the World's
OL,8,FStrongest Masters Championships in
OL,9,FFlorida.
OL,11,FJames Merry, who lifts Atlas stones
OL,12,Fthat weigh up to 200kg (31st 7lb),
OL,13,Fadmitted he was "still shocked" after
OL,14,Fhe received an invitation to take part
OL,15,Fin the competition in November.
OL,17,FThe 41-year-old engineer from
OL,18,FWellingborough, Northamptonshire,
OL,19,Fsecured his place when he won England's
OL,20,FStrongest Masters (40+) last year.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,368,360,200,160,0,100
